From 49a8856b301250b4fce2a0637ee5c13f52106fbb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 12:59:47 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 115/116] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali-oneplus-iceland: keep the
 hall sensor's supply on

The cover's hall sensor on TLMM 98 is powered from L1B. Linux never
voted the rail on: it has no consumer, and another master's vote kept it
on while the SoC was awake. Once the SoC reached CX collapse in s2idle
that vote went away, the sensor's output dropped and came back, and
every sleep ended after half a second on the lid's wake-on-open
interrupt with the cover open.

On the stock firmware the ADSP's sensor hub owns the hall sensor and
powers L1B (its I/O rail) while the sensor runs; the stock device tree
gives Linux the rail at 1.8 V in AUTO mode without ever enabling it.
Here Linux reads the switch through gpio-keys, so keep the rail on.
Voltage and mode stay at stock's values.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
index 816ca3b82..40492d32e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
@@ -538,6 +538,12 @@ vreg_bob2: bob2 {
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
 		};
 
+		/*
+		 * The supply of the cover's hall sensor (BU52053NVX on TLMM 98, the
+		 * gpio-keys lid). On stock the ADSP's sensor hub owns that sensor and
+		 * powers the rail; here Linux reads the switch, so keep the rail on
+		 * for the wake on open, also when the SoC collapses CX in s2idle.
+		 */
 		vreg_l1b_1p8: ldo1 {
 			regulator-name = "vreg_l1b_1p8";
 			regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
@@ -546,6 +552,7 @@ vreg_l1b_1p8: ldo1 {
 			regulator-allow-set-load;
 			regulator-allowed-modes = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_LPM
 						   RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_AUTO>;
+			regulator-always-on;
 		};
 
 		vreg_l2b_3p0: ldo2 {
